  meta wk=7 who=B ph=core
  needs S09
  out figures/structural_sensitivity.png
  chk file figures/structural_sensitivity.png
  orig esr_analysis/plot_structural_sensitivity.py

T S15 S code "Minimal representative set covering >=90% of conformational diversity"
  help Smallest list of medoid entries (QC-pass if possible) whose clusters cover 90% of diversity, with a one-line justification per entry. If 90% is not reachable under QC, say so and show the number.
  meta wk=7 who=B ph=core
  needs S12 R04
  out results/representative_set.csv
  chk csv results/representative_set.csv rows>=1 cols=entry_id,justification
  orig esr_analysis/representative_set.py
  src desc 10 deliverables

T S16 S code "Measure H12 position per chain after core fit (keep every chain)"
  help RMSD of H12 residues 538-547 versus the reference after the core fit; this is the agonist/antagonist signal. Keep every chain: no shared H12 Calpha -> h12_rmsd blank and h12_label not_modelled; fewer than 10 shared -> partial; otherwise complete. Add h12_mean_b and h12_b_group from K03 so a reader sees how mobile H12 is. Large values are reported next to n_h12_ca and never filtered.
  meta wk=4 who=B ph=core
  needs S03 K03
  out results/h12_metric.csv
  chk csv results/h12_metric.csv rows>=700 cols=entry_id,chain_key,n_h12_ca,h12_rmsd,h12_label,h12_mean_b,h12_b_group nonempty=chain_key,h12_label
  src desc 3.2, 5.1; professor notes 2026-10-18

T S17 S run "Clean coordinate files: receptor chain + its ligand of interest"
  help Write one PDB per eligible chain with only that protein chain and its ligand(s) of interest (no waters, ions, additives, partner chains). For pockets (P2Rank), all-atom checks and PyMOL figures; the Calpha RMSD does not need it. Save the script in scripts/.
  meta wk=3 who=B ph=core
  needs Q18
  tool gemmi or biopython
  out data/clean/
  chk glob data/clean/*.pdb >=700
  chk cmd ! grep -lq "HOH" data/clean/*.pdb

