# ===================== EXTENDED ANALYSES, FINAL RUN (phase ext, Y tasks) =====================
# Plan: docs/PLAN_EXTENDED.md. Professor (last meeting): go beyond the description; many clustering methods with
# compactness; auto-selected chemistry clustering; outliers vs quality vs experimental conditions; colour-by plots;
# "why are there two clusters". Keep-all: every one of the 788 matrix chains is used in every full run; tier A / other
# subsets are sensitivity runs next to the full run. Outputs: scripts/ext_*.py, results/ext/, figures/ext/ (200 dpi PNG
# + SVG). Frozen outputs of earlier tasks are read, never rewritten. Seed 42. Ligand action labels (Q10/Q11) are done by a
# teammate by hand: no Y task drafts them; only the 7 evidence-supported block-07 labels are used, all else "unlabelled".

T Y01 S code "Shared style, one cluster palette, figure-card registry, safe PyMOL runner"
  help One module with loaders of the frozen inputs, the validated cluster palette used by every figure, 200 dpi PNG+SVG saving and a figure-card registry; plus the PyMOL wrapper with faulthandler, timeout and output checks.
